# TypeScript Extension Conventions

- Keep strict TypeScript enabled; do not use `any` to bypass extension APIs.
- Define runtime message contracts in `src/shared/contracts.ts`.
- Keep content-script runtime dependencies minimal and never import signing code.
- Validate all user-controlled relay URLs and imported keys.
- Handle rejected Chrome messages and relay operations with actionable UI errors.
- Use type-only imports where values are unnecessary.
- Keep parsing and aggregation logic pure so it can be unit tested.
- Add tests when changing event validation, aggregation, or cache semantics.
- Use functional React components and accessible labels for popup controls.
- Avoid global CSS in injected UI; keep it inside the panel's Shadow DOM.
